==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Good for early-game farming. 
* Low mastery requirements. 
* Easy to upgrade.
* Abnormally large hitbox.


|'''[Z] Multi-Target Slash'''
* Has a [[stun]] effect.
* Can hit multiple targets.
* Good [[AoE]]. 

|'''[X] Tornado Slash'''
* Can hit multiple targets.
* Also has a stun effect.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Cannot hit [[Blade]] users.
* No mobility moves.
* Lack of range with both moves.
* Has low M1 damage, like most [[First Sea]] swords.

|'''[Z] Multi-Target Slash'''
* Has high knockback, making it unsuitable for grinding.
* Terrible range.
* Despite turning invisible the ability does not provide Invincibility Frames.

|'''[X] Tornado Slash'''
* Also has high knockback, making it harder to grind [[NPCs|Enemies]].
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* The [[Cookie Crafter]]s in the [[Sea of Treats]] use the Wardens Sword.
* {{Ability|X}} is similar to [[Blizzard]]'s X move, {{Ability|Blizzard|X}}.
* The item description states that the Wardens Sword has a ring, but due to the revamped model, The ring is now gone.
* Despite the [[Swords|sword]] being called the "Wardens Sword", before [[Updates/30|Update 30]], it actually dropped from the [[Chief Warden]], not the [[Warden]] himself, who used to use the [[Dual Katana]].

